---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/case-study.css';
import BackArrow from '../components/BackArrow.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About this demo | Arka Pradana" description="The people, brands, research and campaigns in this fictional marketing portfolio were created to demonstrate a website experience.">
  <div class="demo-page">
    <section class="demo-hero"><a class="case-back" href="/"><BackArrow /> Back to the portfolio</a><p class="case-kicker">About this demo</p><h1>Made up.<br />Built with intent.</h1><p>A fictional person. Three imagined brands. A real demonstration of how a portfolio can tell a story.</p></section>
    <section class="demo-details">
      <article><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h2>The person and the work.</h2><p>Arka Pradana is a fictional brand and growth strategist. His identity, career history and project roles were created for this website concept. Aeru, Kala Form and Sora Coast are fictional concept brands, not clients of the website creator.</p><p>The case studies demonstrate a possible approach to positioning, campaign strategy and acquisition planning. No campaign placements, customer interviews, enquiries, product sales or bookings described here have taken place.</p></div></article>
      <article><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h2>The images and the evidence.</h2><p>The portrait, product and destination images are AI-generated concept artwork. They illustrate a fictional visual world; they are not photographs documenting a real person, location or production. Campaign layouts and strategy materials are original illustrative mockups.</p><p>Audience insights and research summaries are simulated assumptions. They are shown as starting points to validate, not evidence from actual respondents or proprietary client work. Arka is not credited with producing the photographs or films.</p></div></article>
      <article><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h2>The numbers.</h2><p>The After Hours dashboard uses synthetic data to explain a measurement framework. Scenario A and Scenario B are independent planning examples, not before-and-after results, performance claims or a completed experiment.</p><p>Scenario A models 240 leads from 12,000 sessions, or 2%. Scenario B models 360 leads from 12,000 sessions, or 3%. Neither scenario describes real campaign traffic.</p><a class="demo-text-link" href="/marketing-scenarios.json" download>Download the synthetic dataset <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
      <article><span aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h2>The materials.</h2><p>This site uses Barlow Condensed and Manrope, distributed under the SIL Open Font License. Font sources and license copies are retained with the project. The campaign artwork is generated specifically for this concept rather than borrowed from a real brand.</p><p>Lando Norris’s website was named as a reference for immersive scrolling and cinematic pacing. This project has its own fictional identity, campaign content and implementation; it is not affiliated with Lando Norris or a motorsport team.</p></div></article>
      <article><span aria-hidden="true">05</span><div><h2>The contact experience.</h2><p>This is a portfolio showcase. Campaign calls to action are static mockups. The project brief builder turns the details you enter into a downloadable text file on your device. Nothing is transmitted or saved to a server, and no enquiry is represented as a sent message.</p><p>A real business contact can be added by the website owner when this showcase is prepared for client presentations.</p></div></article>
    </section>
    <a class="demo-return" href="/#work"><span>Back to the concepts</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
